Still unfinished: physical Wi-Fi, TLS, full web standards and multimedia,
preemption/SMP/process isolation, general filesystem feature sets, installed
boot registration, authenticated Internet updates, large guest files and a
full IDE debugger/project system. Do not claim ideal or universal operation.

25NOVEMBER2026 - ZERO WEB0.15PREVIEW

Completed: original Zero HTML tree, CSS cascade, bounded JavaScript profile,
block/inline rasterizer, own Zpix export and Linux/Windows GUI local preview.
Own checks: DOM170, CSS151, JavaScript320, pipeline35;676per host passed native
Linux and Windows/Wine. Independent integration67assertions passed. GUI10cases
per host plus actual final-browser scrolling/close and exact pixel comparison.
76build stages/72artifacts reproduced exactly by the freshly built builder.
Unchanged0.14boot/guest assets are identical; user data disk hashes unchanged.
Source browser/engine/web.zero is generated by own compose.zero. All new
implementation and project tests are Zero; cancelled Python worker removed.

Not done: Internet fetching/TLS for the new engine, full HTML/CSS/ECMAScript,
external scripts/styles, media, guest runtime integration, native Windows
hardware. This is not an all-sites browser or completed Chromium rewrite.
Shared-chat snapshot currently exposes material gathering, not a final idea
list. The new personal library link requires sign-in and supplies no readable
file in this workspace; its contents have not been claimed read or implemented.
GitHub publication target: https://github.com/newmokee-gif/Zero . The owner
created the public repository and requested GPL; original source and programs
are distributed under GNU GPL version3only (GPL-3.0-only). LICENSE contains the
unchanged official license, also supplied as LICENSE.ztext. The GitHub README
is publication metadata; implementation remains Zero/Ezero. Release materials
include system media, all native Linux/Windows tools and language compilers,
guest applications and complete corresponding source. No private data disks
or personal correspondence are part of the public source package.
